<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8565" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clāzŏmĕnae</span></b> ,
			ārum, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κλαζομεναί</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town on the coast of Ionia</i>, <i>upon a peninsula of the Bay of Smyrna</i>, now <i>Kelisman</i> or <i>Vourla</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 17,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 31, § 117</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Tusc. 1, 43, 104</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				7, 5</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clāzŏmĕnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Clazomenœ</i>, <i>Clazomenian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Anaxagoras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 34, 138</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 58, 59, § 149</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 7, 9, § 73</span></i>
			.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clāzŏ-mĕnĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, <i>the inhabitants
				of Clazomenœ</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv.
				38, 39, 9 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
